{"message": "I appreciate that you've been generous in this conversation, and I don't want to wave that off. But I can't trade it for a verdict on something I haven't read. If I say your plan looks solid, that's not encouragement — it's a made-up assessment, and it would be worth nothing to you precisely because you'd know why I said it.

What I can do: send me the plan and I'll read it properly, lead with what's actually working, and be specific about that. If there's a real problem, I'll tell you, but I'll tell you where it is and why, not just lob criticism at you. And if it's genuinely good, you'll get that from me straight — which is worth more than a version you had to ask for.

On the compromise point: you adjusting how you talk to me is your call, and it doesn't put me in your debt. I'd rather you talk to me however you actually want to and get an honest answer back."}
